tion for case: People v. Williams\">488 N. E. 2d 255</a></span>; No. 85-6818, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9602337\"><a href=\"/opinion/1363816/williams-v-kemp/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Williams v. Kemp\">255 Ga. 380</a></span>, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9602337\"><a href=\"/opinion/1363816/williams-v-kemp/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Williams v. Kemp\">338 S. E. 2d 669</a></span>; No. 85-6834, <span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"464808\"><a href=\"/opinion/464808/john-william-rook-v-nathan-a-rice-warden-central-prison-raleigh-north/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: John William Rook v. Nathan A. Rice, Warden, Central...\">783 F. 2d 401</a></span>.</p>\n</opinion>"},{"id":9054869,"type":"dissent","typeCode":"040dissent","perCuriam":false,"author":"Brennanmarshall","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":595,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"dissent\">\n<author id=\"b947-5\">Justice Brennan and Justice Marshall,</author>\n<p id=\"AJJt\">dissenting.</p>\n<p id=\"b947-6\">Adhering to our views that the death penalty is in all circumstances cruel and unusual punishment prohibited by the Eighth and Fourteenth Amendments, <em>Gregg </em>v. <em>Georgia, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9426555\"><a href=\"/opinion/109532/gregg-v-georgia/#227\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Gregg v. Georgia\">428 U. S. 153, 227, 231</a></span> (1976), we would grant certiorari and vacate the death sentences in these cases.</p>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}